@iholder101, thanks for the reply. 

1. For diretories created for empty-dir, there should be no mountpoints.

// Not all volumes were removed, so don't clean up the pod directory yet. It is likely
// that there are still mountpoints or files left which could cause removal of the pod
// directory to fail below.

2. EmptyDir::TearDownAt was called indeeded, but the not-yet-exiting process of init containers created the empty-dir again and put some files under this dir.

3. And then the empty-dir and its sub-dirs are left undeleted with following logs, and the disk will be filled up eventually:
